/-!
# Complete Boolean certificate for Held elementary extensions

All 23 × 1024 branches of the literal extension checker return true. The
row certificates use kernel reduction on the previously certified permutation
tables; blocks of 32 share computation without a large monolithic reduction.
The quotient-and-remainder assembly covers every original normal-form index.

This theorem has no mathematical premises. Together with `branchAction_eq`,
it supplies the Boolean premise of `eq_target_of_branchCheck` in `Criterion.lean`.
The separate exact-node-membership certificate is still needed to assemble
the normal elementary extension theorem.

